%description:

Tcp.initialCwnd:invalid -- a value below 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts 0 and more; the NED says "0: initialWindow".

The classes: zero (0, the default: initialWindow decides), segments (1 and more), invalid
(below 0). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase::getInitialWindow(), and the check in
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables().

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialCwnd
%# class: invalid
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialCwnd
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialCwndInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialCwnd = -1    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
initialCwnd must be 0 or more, but it is -1
